      "writtenOn": "2016-07-04T02:33:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the purge is only used by the client, which can purge the mapping base on domain_id/public_id/local_id/type, or a combination of the above ids.\n\n\nplease refer to: \nhttps://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/cmd/cli.py#L572\n\n\nif we invalidate part of the region based on the filter, it will be become a little complex for the code to implemented.\n\n\nAs it will be very rare condition for user to purge mapping using client. and invalidate all cache, just like become to the situation like no cache used or restart keystone, and after some operation about the id mappings, it will be cache again.\n\n\nSo comparing to the complexity of the implementation based on the purge filter, I think it\u0027s acceptable to invalidate all cache.",
